From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:01:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: muxes: i2c-hotplug-gpio: Fix the parent adapter lookup

of_parse_phandle() and of_find_i2c_adapter_by_node() return NULL when
they find nothing, not an error pointer, so a missing i2c-parent or a
parent adapter that has not been registered yet went past the IS_ERR()
checks and probe dereferenced a NULL adapter. Return -ENODEV for the
missing property and defer while the parent adapter is not there, like
i2c-mux-pinctrl does.

of_find_i2c_adapter_by_node() also takes no reference on the parent's
module, which i2c_put_adapter() then drops. Use
of_get_i2c_adapter_by_node(), which takes both references that
i2c_put_adapter() releases.

The parent can come later, for example an i2c-gpio bus built as a
module.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-hotplug-gpio.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-hotplug-gpio.c b/drivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-hotplug-gpio.c
index 7f56964e285e..9688d1be9242 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-hotplug-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-hotplug-gpio.c
@@ -179,14 +179,14 @@ static int i2c_hotplug_gpio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	priv->dev = &pdev->dev;
 
 	parent_np = of_parse_phandle(pdev->dev.of_node, "i2c-parent", 0);
-	if (IS_ERR(parent_np))
-		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(parent_np),
+	if (!parent_np)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -ENODEV,
 				     "cannot parse i2c-parent\n");
 
-	parent = of_find_i2c_adapter_by_node(parent_np);
+	parent = of_get_i2c_adapter_by_node(parent_np);
 	of_node_put(parent_np);
-	if (IS_ERR(parent))
-		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(parent),
+	if (!parent)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
 				     "failed to get parent I2C adapter\n");
 	priv->parent = parent;
 
-- 
